.TH V23-FORTUNE 1
.SH NAME
v23/fortune \- Vanadium RPC fortune client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B v23/fortune
[
.B -a
.I addr
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I V23/fortune
creates a client principal, dials
.I addr
(default
.BR tcp!127.0.0.1!3245 )
with ACL
.BR ... ,
invokes method
.B Get
with an empty argument, and prints the returned string.
.PP
Requires a running
.IR v23-fortuned (8)
(or compatible
.IR v23-rpc (2)
server).
.PP
.B /net
must be available in the name space (bind Inferno’s network
before starting
.IR emu (1)
clients that dial).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/v23/fortune.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR v23-fortuned (8),
.IR v23-rpc (2),
.IR v23-intro (2),
.IR dial (2)
.SH BUGS
.IP \(bu
End-to-end TCP smoke tests have hung when
.B /net
was missing or mis-bound; the client does not time out dials.
.IP \(bu
ACL is hard-coded to
.BR ... ;
no CLI for roots or patterns.
.IP \(bu
Only the
.B Get
method is used; no
.B Add
client.
.SH TODO
.IP \(bu
Flags for blessing name, ACL, timeout, and method selection.
.IP \(bu
Print peer blessings after handshake for debugging.
